        <br>
        <br><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small> </small></font>
        <br><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>4087 Posts</small></font></td>
        <td bgcolor="white" colspan="2" valign="top"><img src="icon_posticon.gif" border="0" hspace="3"><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1">Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;12/19/2001&nbsp;:&nbsp; 10:26:31</font>
        
		&nbsp;<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=142"><img src="icon_profile.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Show Profile" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>
        
        &nbsp;<a href="http://" target="_blank"><img src="icon_homepage.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Visit draknelle's Homepage" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>


        <hr noshade size="1">

        <font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> The time was indeed excellent as Gadal has stated . :-)) I am ever more enthralled with the alert and treacherous mind our mighty High Elf has exhibited on the two raids I have been under his guidance and expertise. Talk aobut controlled chaos! that was it! All turned out well, even though one piece rotted but whew! try running that show with all us crazies ( helloo Wubbie :-)) and keep on top of it all . Heh! try fighting, and rolling on a piece of armor some time, what a kick!!. Nuff said. Thank you so much Loral and all for treating this Blu babe to a grand time. *hugs</P><P> <a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td bgcolor="ccccff" valign="top">

		<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=22">

		<font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><b>Soulsender</a>
        </b></font>

        <br><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>Officer</small></font>

        <br><img src=icon_star_green.gif border=0><img src=icon_star_green.gif border=0><img src=icon_star_green.gif border=0><img src=icon_star_green.gif border=0>
        <br>
        <br><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small> </small></font>
        <br><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>4191 Posts</small></font></td>
        <td bgcolor="ccccff" colspan="2" valign="top"><img src="icon_posticon.gif" border="0" hspace="3"><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1">Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;12/19/2001&nbsp;:&nbsp; 11:09:54</font>
        
		&nbsp;<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=22"><img src="icon_profile.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Show Profile" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>
        
        &nbsp;<a href="http://" target="_blank"><img src="icon_homepage.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Visit Soulsender's Homepage" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>


        <hr noshade size="1">

        <font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Without doubt, this was the most exciting and enjoyable raid I have even been on. Rather than the static monotony of pull after pull, by initiating the Dwarf Traitor quest I actually felt part of a massive adventure deep in enemy territory. The coordination of the groups was amazing to behold...taking down the Brothers amid a room of spawning badass giants. It was also a treat to watch Loral tweak his battle plans as additional information and experience was gained.</P><P>Of course coming away with some phat loot (with special thanks to Wubs) also served to round out the evening <img src=icon_smile.gif border=0 align=middle>.</P><P>"Incredible" says it all...well, all except "when are we going back!?!!"</P><P>Soulsender Bloodfiend<BR>49 Iksar SK<BR>Lizard of Eternal Officer Training<BR>Healers United</P><P><BR> <a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td bgcolor="white" valign="top">

		<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=5">

